<meta type=article title="Math environments + <math> long-form fixture (Phase 2 slice 2b)">
</meta>

<section | Long-form `<math>`>

The `<math>` long-form is semantically equivalent to the `<$$>` display-math
sigil; both render block-level LaTeX via KaTeX. Use the long-form when the
source is multi-line or when explicit tag bounds aid readability.

<math>
\sum_{i=1}^{n} x_i = X
</math>

<section | Matrix>

The `<matrix>` env renders a LaTeX matrix. The handler wraps the body in
`\begin{matrix}...\end{matrix}` before passing to KaTeX (wrap-inside
convention).

<matrix>
1 & 2 \\
3 & 4
</matrix>

<section | Cases>

The `<cases>` env renders a piecewise definition.

<cases>
x^2 & \text{if } x \ge 0 \\
-x^2 & \text{if } x < 0
</cases>

<section | Aligned equations>

The `<align>` env renders multi-line aligned equations via KaTeX's
`aligned` env (the supported equivalent of LaTeX's top-level `align` env).

<align>
x^2 + y^2 &= z^2 \\
a + b &= c
</align>

<section | Eqnarray (LaTeX-compat)>

The `<eqnarray>` env exists for LaTeX-source compatibility — authors
copying `\begin{eqnarray}...` source from a LaTeX document have a
matching enscribe tag. Renders via the same KaTeX `aligned` env.

<eqnarray>
f(x) &=& x^2 \\
g(x) &=& 2x
</eqnarray>

This fixture exercises all five sub-slice-2b tags end-to-end via the
extended `math.js` handler. The existing `<$>` / `<$$>` sigil snapshots
(documents 4, 5, 11) must be unchanged — the per-tagname dispatch path
preserves the sigil branches exactly. Numbering output is asserted only
for the display-math sigil (in its existing fixtures); the new tags are
not yet in `NUMBERED_TAGNAMES`, so they don't receive equation-number
spans — that integration is regular-vocabulary work, out of scope here.
